    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bactericidal beta-lactams (mechanism unknown, perhaps activating autolytic enzymes that destroy the cell wall)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Mostly hypersensitivity:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " immediate (anaphylaxis, urticaria, angioedema) or delayed (serum sickness, rashes, exfoliative dermatitis). High doses: seizures (esp. renal insufficiency); nephritis, C. difficile diarrhea, Coombs+ hemolytic anemia, leukopenia, thrombocytopenia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Serious prior allergic reaction to a penicillin. Most patients who report penicillin allergy don't react on re-exposure; with a vague or inconsistent history and no effective or convenient alternative, skin testing may be done."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Probenecid blocks renal tubular secretion and raises penicillin levels."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
